From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:32:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] nemotron: router logits of passes over 32 rows run on
 128-row by 128-expert register tiles

tf_nemo_router_tiles stages two 32-input steps of 128 rows and 128 experts; a thread keeps 8 rows by 8 experts in
registers and runs every logit's fma chain over its slice in input order, so the partials keep their bits. Glue.logits
picks the router kernel for Nano's and Super's routers alike: windows up to 16 rows keep tf_nemo_router_rows, windows of
17 to 32 rows and unaligned rows tf_nemo_router, longer aligned passes the tiles. At Super's router (4,096 inputs,
512 experts, 8 slices) a GB10 runs tf_nemo_router in 45-47 us at 17 to 32 rows against the tiles' 50-51 us, and in
66 us at 40 rows, 174 us at 128 and 409 us at 300 against 51, 54 and 110 us. `tf-cuda-test glue` compares the tiles
with tf_nemo_router and the host reference at 33 and 300 rows (4,100 against tf_nemo_router), and a 32-row window.
